      "level": 2,
      "text": "2.3 What moved"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "APAC: +24.3% to $12,343k.",
        "North America: +17.1% to $6,038k.",
        "EMEA: +7.6% to $3,787k."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "2.4 Regional commentary"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "North America"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "North America delivered $6,038k, +17.1% year over year and 27% of group revenue. Its best quarter was Q2 ($1,567k) and its weakest Q1 ($1,447k), a spread of 8%. That is 2.1% points behind the group, so we are reviewing the plan for next year."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "EMEA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "EMEA delivered $3,787k, +7.6% year over year and 17% of group revenue. Its best quarter was Q2 ($1,005k) and its weakest Q3 ($911k), a spread of 9%. That is 11.6% points behind the group, so we are reviewing the plan for next year."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "APAC"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "APAC delivered $12,343k, +24.3% year over year and 56% of group revenue. Its best quarter was Q4 ($3,162k) and its weakest Q3 ($3,029k), a spread of 4%. That is 5.2% points ahead of the group, so it is a candidate for more investment."
    },
    {
